# No hardcodes, brief path

Do not invent string/number literals for things the project already names. Reach the target with the shortest existing API.

- Keys, statuses, roles, permissions, log events, error codes, environments → enums (`MessageKey`, `LogEvent`, `Permission`, `EnvironmentType`, …).
- User-visible text → `MessageKey` + localization files (`en.yml`, …). Never inline messages.
- Project name, version, URLs, timeouts, paths, secrets → `AppConfiguration` (`config.project()`, `config.jwt()`, …). Never `@Value`.
- Reuse existing core services instead of a new helper that only wraps one call.
- Skip extra variables, wrappers, and comments that do not change behavior.

```java
// ❌ BAD
cache.put("user:" + id, user, Duration.ofMinutes(10));
throw new NotFoundException("User not found"); // new literal, new text

// ✅ GOOD
cache.put(CacheKey.USER.of(id), user, config.cache().userTtl());
throw new NotFoundException(MessageKey.USER_NOT_FOUND);
```
